Behind the Scene: How Pods Get Placed on Nodes

Ever wondered how your pods end up on specific nodes? That’s the job of the Kubernetes Scheduler.

What It Does?
- Watches for unscheduled pods
- Evaluates available nodes
- Matches pods to the best-fitting node based on:
  + Resource requests (CPU, memory)
  + Taints & tolerations
  + Node selectors / affinity rules

Understanding the Kubernetes Scheduler provides insight into how your applications are deployed and managed, allowing you to optimize your Pod specifications for better performance, resilience, and resource usage.
